  {
   "etapa": "explicar",
   "piezas": [
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Seeing someone again",
     "texto": [
      "When you haven't seen someone for a while: **Lâu rồi không gặp anh!** = Long time no see! (lâu = a long time; rồi = already).",
      "**Dạo này anh có khỏe không?** = How are you doing lately? If there's no news, you reply **Tôi bình thường.** = Normal, as always.",
      "To introduce someone politely: **Tôi xin giới thiệu với anh, đây là Liên, bạn tôi.** = Let me introduce you to Liên, my friend."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Vietnamese names",
     "texto": [
      "A Vietnamese name usually has three parts: **surname + middle name + given name**. In **Nguyễn Văn Hùng**, Nguyễn is the surname and **Hùng** is the name everyone uses.",
      "In everyday speech it's common to use the first name with a form of address in front: **anh Hùng, ông Hùng, chị Lan, cô Hoa**. The surname alone usually isn't the friendly way to call someone; usage depends on the situation.",
      "Names mean something: Hùng (brave), Dũng (valiant), Cường (strong); Lan (orchid), Hoa (flower), Liên (lotus), Tuyết (snow), Nguyệt (moon), Hương (fragrance)."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    }
   ]
  },
